[{"id":"vr-predict-hold","itemId":"valid-ready","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"This is lesson 10.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">vr_reg</code>, a register of one place, empty at the start, between a source and a sink. A value moves at a rising edge where its valid and its ready are both 1 just before it. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>A value moves in at the edges that start cycles 1, 4 and 6, where <code class=\"nobreak\">in_valid</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">in_ready</code> are both 1 just before them, and out at the edges of cycles 3, 5 and 8, where <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">out_ready</code> are. So <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> is 1 in cycles 1 and 2, 4, 6 and 7. In cycle 6 the sink is not ready, so at cycle 7's edge the value stays.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"vr-hold","source":"hdl/level-10/vr_reg/vr_reg_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":9,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"vr_reg_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_valid","path":"vr_reg_tb.in_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_ready","path":"vr_reg_tb.in_ready","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[4,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[6,"0"],[7.5,"1"]]},{"label":"out_ready","path":"vr_reg_tb.out_ready","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[7.5,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"out_valid","path":"vr_reg_tb.out_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[8,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","0","1","1","0"]}]},"answer":"out_valid","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"vr-predict-stream","itemId":"valid-ready","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">vr_reg</code>, lesson 10.1's register of one place, empty at the start. <code class=\"nobreak\">in_ready</code> is not drawn: it is 1 when the register is empty or its value leaves at the same edge. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">in_ready</code> is 1 when the register is empty or its value is leaving. A value comes in at cycle 1's edge. In cycle 1 the register is full and the sink is not ready, so the source's next value waits, and <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> stays 1. At the edges of cycles 3 and 8 one value leaves as the next comes in, so it stays 1; at cycle 4's nothing moves. At the edges of cycles 5 and 9 the last value leaves with none behind it: 0. Values come in again at the edges of cycles 7 and 10.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"vr-stream","source":"hdl/level-10/vr_reg/vr_reg_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":11,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"vr_reg_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"],[10,"1"],[10.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_valid","path":"vr_reg_tb.in_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9.5,"1"]]},{"label":"out_ready","path":"vr_reg_tb.out_ready","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[9.5,"0"],[10.5,"1"]]},{"label":"out_valid","path":"vr_reg_tb.out_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"],[9,"0"],[10,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","1","1","1","0","0","1","1","0","1"]}]},"answer":"out_valid"},{"id":"vr-find-bug","itemId":"valid-ready","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">vr_reg_bug</code> should pass every value from its source to its sink once, in order, as lesson 10.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">vr_reg</code> does. Its testbench, the one <code class=\"nobreak\">vr_reg</code> passes, fails: where the sink should get 3, it gets 4. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">out_data</code> must change only when a value moves in: at an edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">in_valid</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">in_ready</code> are both 1. As written it takes <code class=\"nobreak\">in_data</code> whenever <code class=\"nobreak\">in_valid</code> is 1. While the register holds 3 and the sink is not ready, <code class=\"nobreak\">in_ready</code> is 0 and the source waits with 4, but the register takes 4 anyway. 3 is lost, and 4 comes out twice.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-10/vr_reg_bug/vr_reg_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// One register between a source and a sink that use valid and ready. A","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// value moves in at a rising edge where in_valid and in_ready are both 1,","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// and out at one where out_valid and out_ready are both 1. The register","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// holds one value; in_ready says it has room for another at this edge:","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// it is empty, or its value is leaving now.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"vr_reg_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":